---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../lib/siteConfig';

/**
 * Privacy policy (§6, Phase C7; launch form 2026-08-04) — describes the
 * privacy-by-architecture reality (CLAUDE.md hard constraint 5): no
 * cookies, no forms, no tracking, no health information. Counsel
 * reviews post-launch (operator acceptance, DECISIONS 2026-08-04).
 */
---

<LegalLayout
  heading="Privacy"
  title="Privacy | Needle Girlie"
  description="How needlegirlie.com handles privacy: no cookies, no forms, no tracking, no health information collected."
>
  <p>
    Needle Girlie respects the privacy of every visitor, and this website
    is built to collect as little as possible.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This website sets no cookies.</li>
    <li>It contains no forms and collects no personal information.</li>
    <li>It uses no advertising or retargeting pixels and no third-party trackers.</li>
    <li>
      It currently runs no analytics. If privacy-preserving, cookieless
      analytics are added later, they will measure aggregate page visits
      only, and this page will be updated first.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hosting and technical logs</h2>
  <p>
    Like nearly every website, needlegirlie.com is served by hosting
    infrastructure (Microsoft Azure) that produces standard technical
    logs — requested pages, timestamps, and network addresses — as part
    of operating and securing the service. Those logs are technical
    operations data held by the hosting platform; Needle Girlie does not
    use them to identify visitors.
  </p>

  <h2>Health information</h2>
  <p>
    This website collects no health information. It has no forms, no
    chat, and no patient portal. Conversations about care happen in
    consultation and at appointments, not through this website.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website collects no personal information from anyone, including
    children.
  </p>

  <h2>Where you leave this website</h2>
  <p>
    Some links open other companies' services, and their privacy
    practices apply there, not this policy:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Booking happens on Vagaro, a third-party scheduling service.</li>
    <li>Skincare purchases happen on the Skinbetter Science storefront.</li>
    <li>Social links open Facebook, Instagram, and Yelp.</li>
    <li>"Get directions" opens your map provider.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes — for example, if privacy-preserving,
    cookieless analytics are added — the new version will be posted on
    this page with an updated effective date.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be directed to Needle Girlie by phone
    at <a href={siteConfig.phoneTel}>{siteConfig.phone}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
